## 2. Why It Was Built

1. **Security First**: Code execution platforms face hostile users. We must establish identity (Authentication) and permissions (Authorization) before allowing any user to submit code or administer problems.
2. **Data Privacy (Hidden Test Cases)**: If regular users could query all test cases via the API, they could write code that simply hard-codes outputs for every test case. We enforce at the service layer that only `isSample: true` test cases are returned to regular users.
3. **Controller-Service-Repository Pattern**: Keeping business logic in `services/` makes our codebase modular, testable without HTTP mocks, and clean for technical interview discussions.

