## 5. Important Trade-offs

| Decision | Alternative Considered | Trade-off & Justification |
|---|---|---|
| **JWT in Authorization header** | Server-side sessions in Redis | JWT requires no database lookup per request (faster, stateless). Trade-off: Token revocation before expiration requires a denylist. For our scale, a 7-day token is optimal. |
| **bcrypt (10 rounds)** | Argon2 or PBKDF2 | bcrypt is battle-tested, standard across Node.js backend interviews, and resilient against GPU cracking. 10 rounds takes ~100ms per hash, balancing safety and server CPU usage. |
| **Cascade delete on Problems** | Soft deletes (`isDeleted = true`) | Cascade delete (`onDelete: Cascade` in PostgreSQL) keeps the schema simple and prevents orphan test cases. Soft deletes complicate queries with `where: { isDeleted: false }`. |

